{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city","id":1508459,"title":"Have you Defended a City?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-15T10:38:39-07:00","id":1508459,"title":"Have you Defended a City?","content":"It is one thing to defend a single building or small territory, but it is another to defend a town or city. Back in the day cities had walls as a default defensive measure against mortal armies, which in turn kept the shifters and other supernatural threats if not at bay, at least they had to consider them in their plans.<br /> <br /> But what about in the modern world? If you are a Prince/Baron/Cardinal and you influence the mortal world for a century or more, how do you guide the development of the city to promote ease of defense? The fluff states that every city has hordes of shifters circling in the unincorporated areas just waiting for kindred to step a toe outside of the city limits. Likewise, every splat seems to have a faction that lives in the same cities, so how do you set things up to counter them?<br /> <br /> The fluff is kind of obsessed with saying that vampires are city dwellers with loads of influence, endless resources, and that their enemies are legion. But somehow once the mortals stopped building walls around their cities, it seems that the vampires just gave up trying to do anything that dealt with known threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T11:20:36-07:00","id":1508463,"title":"","content":"My biggest concern in a vampire siege scenario is not the enemy, for they don't know shit about me, but rather the other vampires who are meant to be on my side, who know me better. <br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to shifters, Vampires don't need to do anything, because the lupines are certain of their own defeat. Werewolves can win battles, they might choose to risk targeting an exceptional Wyrm spreader, but they know they'll lose wars. In a modern city, with such massive population counts in comparison to medieval cities, it's extraordinarily easy for vampires to restore any losses they take. Like if they lost 50 vampires one night they could regain 50 before the night is over if they so chose to do so. Werewolves on the otherhand have a relative replenishment rate of, say, for every werewolf they get a new one every two or three decades give or take. Nobody can compete with Vampires when it comes to replenishment. Not Ratkin, not mages, not changelings, not anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T12:12:34-07:00","id":1508473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city#post1508459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But somehow once the mortals stopped building walls around their cities, it seems that the vampires just gave up trying to do anything that dealt with known threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I woud say it is partially true<br /> The Herd stopped building walls because walls became obsolete around the time Ottoman canons started to rain destruction to the walls of constantinople...<br /> In the wake of city growth and the ensuing change of defensive strategy, focusing more on the defense of forts around cities, many city walls were demolished. Also, the invention of gunpowder rendered walls less effective, as siege cannons could then be used to blast through walls, allowing armies to simply march through. Today, the presence of former city fortifications can often only be deduced from the presence of ditches, ring roads or parks. Furthermore, some street names hint at the presence of fortifications in times past, for example when words such as &quot;wall&quot; or &quot;glacis&quot; occur. In the 19th century, less emphasis was placed on preserving the fortifications for the sake of their architectural or historical value \u2013 on the one hand, complete fortifications were restored , on the other hand many structures were demolished in an effort to modernize the cities. One exception to this is the &quot;monument preservation&quot; law by the Bavarian King Ludwig I of Bavaria, which led to the nearly complete preservation of many monuments such as the Rothenburg ob der Tauber, N\u00f6rdlingen and Dinkelsb\u00fchl. The countless small fortified towns in the Franconia region were also preserved as a consequence of this edict.<br /> Walls and fortified wall structures were still built in the modern era. They did not, however, have the original purpose of being a structure able to resist a prolonged siege or bombardment. The focus shifted to enable the city to impose tolls on goods and, secondarily, also served to prevent the desertion of soldiers<br /> Additionally, in some countries, different embassies may be grouped together in a single &quot;embassy district&quot;, enclosed by a fortified complex with walls and towers \u2013 this usually occurs in regions where the embassies run a high risk of being target of attacks.<br /> Most of these modern city walls are made of steel and concrete. Vertical concrete plates are put together so as to allow the least space in between them, and are rooted firmly in the ground. The top of the wall is often protruding and beset with barbed wire in order to make climbing them more difficult. These walls are usually built in straight lines and covered by watchtowers at the corners.<br /> BUT<br /> The walls around the cities... diss\u200bapeared and it gave the illusion of freedom - freedom to come and go and the feeling We are Strong and don't need walls to protect us! False senses of security and freedom<br /> The greatest trick the devil ever played <i>was convincing the world that he did not exist</i>\u200b<br /> Like how the lack of walls lull the humans into a false sense of security and freedom - makes them easier to controll<br /> The Walls are there, but not made of stone or wood, steel or concrete. - became invisible and intangible<br /> In reality it is very hard to dissapear or move without a trace or leave a city unnoticed - internet, cameras everywhere... and the City have eyes. The faceless mass of homeless people, poor and miserable souls, urchins nobody see or notice - but the great source of information just to name a few (and those are just the Human methods, be it legal or illegal, the Vampires have their own repetoir to watch their hunting grounds)<br /> In VtM the Lupine are... the Lupine, not the Garou. They are beasts with bestial mindset, intelligent, sure, but ultimatelly beasts. The City to them is strange and frightening, the home turf of the vampires, from their point of view, it is the reverse of the Herd's false sense of security and freedom the lack of walls give - to them I think it shows, these smoothskins and their fanged predators are not afraid, the city is like a growing dark storm with birght lights and loud noises, choking fumes and smell and ther territory is clear<br /> In nature - what the Lupine (and even the Garous) are part of, there are no walls. Predator and Prey know their place, know where are the borders of another<br /> If you play a crossover, Garou are more aware of these but on the deeper spiritual level; in the Umbra a City is a web covered dark and tainted place an wandering in even with a pack is a dangerous and hunting leeches are a sport that have it own consequences, like loosing a park because a vampire decided it is time for revenge and ideal for a parking lot - poking the behive that is the vampires on their home turf simply not worth it since the 17th century - like how the Vampires will not risk an all out war with the Lupine/Garou and in turth over time a carefull balance developed<br /> That balance is part of the &quot;invisible wall&quot;<br /> Defending the city from the dangers of the wild is not hard - that is basically a Cold War with proxy battles (sometimes with arranged ones, if you want to be curel; if you remember the 1988 movie The Adventures of Baron Munchausen with John Neville among other great names - there were a scene where the Sultan and Jonathan Pryce's cruel bureaucrat are talking about how this week a few thousand defenders will die, next, some turks, War is a good business and agreed how to be fought to be benefical to the Leaders - it would be fitting to the World of Darkness if some Vampire Elders, the Prince and the Primogens via letters, or even meeting in person agrees: So we will send time to time troublesome fledglings in to your claws, your youngs could have their victories and honorable battles, trophies in turn you can have these parts with the trees, we build some parks even, and you could send some cubs who ask too many questions in to their honorable deaths you could avange later and blame the bad vampires and humans and keep your positions in your society . On the same note, anyone who wander away or would try to flee our domain or try to come in are fair play, kill them, hunt them have fun; be our Wall of Claws and Fangs that howl in the night! If you come in? Behave, if not, we will smack your noses with a rolled up newspaper so to speak, but we prefer our city, you prefer your forest. Deal? Deal? See you next month )<br /> Defending a Domainfrom a Sabbat Siege? That is the real challenge!<br /> Or a Baali infestation<br /> The real threat to a city are the dangers the walls couldn't and wouldn't protect from even if walls would exist\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T13:49:12-07:00","id":1508484,"title":"","content":"The idea of thirty guys in a city of millions laying siege to thirty other guys hiding in that city of millions has always been strange. It would likely be more of a bunch of little sieges. Even then it would be rough. I mean, have you walked around a city lately? Imagine thirty guys, even with low-level superpowers, trying to lay siege to a skyscrapper without attracting a major human response. Now imagine that's a world of darkness skyscrapper with additional secret defenses. The effort needed to conquer one Ventrue's skyscrapper would be massive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T19:04:32-07:00","id":1508504,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about it, but I've defended and conquered many cities in the 13th century! The modern times are strange to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T19:35:52-07:00","id":1508506,"title":"","content":"I.am ST a siege of Chicago in 1991. It's not about the battle, but a game of cat and mouse between the Sabbat, whose strategy is to infiltrate packs and to use part on those packs and other agents to find information about their rival havens and weaknesses and to sow discord and make the Camarilla agents waste their time and resources.<br /> On the other side is the Prince's agents, who use their human networks to follow leads and hunt the packs they can find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T23:46:39-07:00","id":1508513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508484#post1508484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of thirty guys in a city of millions laying siege to thirty other guys hiding in that city of millions has always been strange. It would likely be more of a bunch of little sieges. Even then it would be rough. I mean, have you walked around a city lately? Imagine thirty guys, even with low-level superpowers, trying to lay siege to a skyscrapper without attracting a major human response. Now imagine that's a world of darkness skyscrapper with additional secret defenses. The effort needed to conquer one Ventrue's skyscrapper would be massive.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is probably the most you'd get of a siege in the traditional sense.<br /> <br /> You don't siege a city in the World of Darkness. You invade a city like you'd invade territory, maybe, but you don't lay siege to it. You siege a building, if anything. Vampires could turn a building into a fortified strong point, like a toll booth castle.<br /> <br /> But as with medieval sieges, taking the fort isn't the only thing an invading force would do. There's also all the stuff outside the fortified strongpoint that the Vampires inside care about. It's why when Sabbat declare a crusade on a city, they save Elysium for last in most cases. You destroy supply lines, sources of income, Domains, things the inhabitants of the city like (ex: art galleries for Toreador). Disrupt feeding grounds and Herds. Maybe even foment enough unrest to make the authorities impose martial law, so suddenly the native Kindred are inconvenienced by curfews, closed shops, and heightened security.<br /> <br /> It's the modern equivalent of burning crops to force the local lord to ride out of his castle to face you.<br /> <br /> <br /> All of this, I think, largely misses the point. Kindred don't do much to defend against Lupines because they aren't much of a threat anymore. In pre-modern times, the wilderness was deep and expansive. Lots of places for wolfmen to hide. Travel was slow going, so there was little hope of escape or outside aid if Lupines started beating down your door. (Or, for that matter, mundane soldiery. War was always a problem, hence why mortals built castle walls).<br /> <br /> In modern times, the maps have been filled in and the forests have retreated from the cancerous growth of suburban sprawl. Kindred continue to tell their childer that horrifying werewolves stalk just beyond the city limits. Partly because Elders are slow to change and retain the fears from their younger days. But those with sense still perpetuate the threat in the minds of Kindred, regardless of how diminished Lupines are, because it serves their interests to keep Neonates where they can be watched. Rather than roaming around the endless rows of single family detached homes, growing broods and carving out Domains beyond the eyes and reach of their &quot;betters&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T05:26:23-07:00","id":1508526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508513#post1508513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the modern equivalent of burning crops to force the local lord to ride out of his castle to face you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry<br /> I have to<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pygLvyDdewU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pygLvyDdewU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pygLvyDdewU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pygLvyDdewU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T16:30:20-07:00","id":1508579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508463#post1508463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to shifters, Vampires don't need to do anything, because the lupines are certain of their own defeat. Werewolves can win battles, they might choose to risk targeting an exceptional Wyrm spreader, but they know they'll lose wars. In a modern city, with such massive population counts in comparison to medieval cities, it's extraordinarily easy for vampires to restore any losses they take. Like if they lost 50 vampires one night they could regain 50 before the night is over if they so chose to do so. Werewolves on the otherhand have a relative replenishment rate of, say, for every werewolf they get a new one every two or three decades give or take. Nobody can compete with Vampires when it comes to replenishment. Not Ratkin, not mages, not changelings, not anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't always work: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508463#post1508463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest concern in a vampire siege scenario is not the enemy, for they don't know shit about me, but rather the other vampires who are meant to be on my side, who know me better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can embrace 50 more vamps a night, but would they fight and die for you? Do you think some would run and hide, or others, betray you so the Lupines may spare them?<br /> <br /> And you're right about Lupines; it will take a long time to replenish their ranks, so, better set up an ambush rather than a siege and or get someone else to siege the city, like an Allied Bombing raid. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T07:38:25-07:00","id":1508632,"title":"","content":"There is a good section on this in <i>Elysium: the Elder Wars</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T10:24:04-07:00","id":1508650,"title":"","content":"I've always understood that Vampire wars are fought akin to gang/criminal wars of which there are legion in popular culture. So I would say that trying to defend a city isn't about defending every inch or knowing everyone who is in a city, as that would most likely be impossible with the small and not very united population that any Cainite community have. Its more about defending key assets and key people while removing the same stuff from the opposition.<br /> <br /> Watch some movies about gangsters in the 1920s, prison gangs or street gangs or what else you've got and you should probably have a decent grasp about how engagements are done. Not massive battles but various hit-and-run attacks, ambushes, bombings and so on which as little risk to your own side as possible and most often against one or a few of the enemy at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:29:39-07:00","id":1508655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city#post1508459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about in the modern world? If you are a Prince/Baron/Cardinal and you influence the mortal world for a century or more, how do you guide the development of the city to promote ease of defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be areas and regions which are definitely friendly, nice, good, and convienient for persons who are regulars and citizens from the area and the city, relatively to being less than ideal or average for beings and persons who would be arriving from outside or acting against usual and common interests and activities of a particular urban region, city, or town.<br /> These qualities might occur and exist also in regard to particular methods, capabilities, decisions, and actions.<br /> <br /> For example there might be designated areas which help and support loyal citizens, defenders, heroes, and diplomats in regard to these and simillar activites : for example relaxation, or social networks, or observation, maybe research, maybe logistics, or entertainment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T15:37:44-07:00","id":1508675,"title":"","content":"Sadly, the Background system in VtM doesn't hold a candle to something like the Manse background in Exalted when it comes to building out a proper defensive structure. <br /> <br /> VtM is setup to produce things like the apartment building from The Raid: Redemption, which has no real defenses other than security cameras and an intercom system. It was the crazy tenants that made the building a fortress.<br /> <br /> The main thing is that after a certain point, real investment in defensive structures takes construction crews rather than just a few vampiric builders. But that in turn means that everyone in the city knows where to go and what to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T01:27:13-07:00","id":1508720,"title":"","content":"Ways a prince could do well in a siege scenario <br /> <br /> 1- Actually be a popular prince that most would agree is the right man in charge. <br /> 2- have friends in the enemy faction <br /> 3- push your enemies into conflict in the name of the greater good/ punish them severely when they &quot;rebel&quot;. Ideally you can also pretend to be fair and also assign your allies easy battles where they can accumulate credit <br /> 4- Be very generous to allies and unaligned parties you can win over, discount and deminish the war achievments of rivals and enemies.<br /> 5- If the Sabbat break the masquerade or too much trouble occurs in rival territory, use this as an excuse to take territory off them and reward an ally. <br /> 6: have shelters prepared beforehand. People will owe you big favours when they retreat into one. <br /> <br /> As for guiding a city for the purpose of defense? <br /> -Encourage lots of glass/shiny surfaces for the purpose of thwarting lasombra. <br /> -Manage a shortlist of likely spots for enemy shelters. <br /> -Have a fairly large area in the city where it's quiet at night and quite difficult to commit crimes, perhaps the oldtown or the finance sector, or somewhere near a well guarded government building. This is a good place to act -business as usual-. Ideally the Prince should be able to put up a strong front. It's not good for the prince to hide, as they're supposed to be leaders who can coordinate things. It's much better to put yourself in an area where the enemy dare not attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T01:51:36-07:00","id":1508723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508675#post1508675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main thing is that after a certain point, real investment in defensive structures takes construction crews rather than just a few vampiric builders. But that in turn means that everyone in the city knows where to go and what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of the usual, normal, prepared, and experienced construction crews another approach could be decided upon. My idea is that it could be attempted that groups of mortal volunteers, maybe standard workers, or honest amateurs could be drafted or employed into various logistics, structures, and terrain related tasks, projects, and activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T07:55:20-07:00","id":1508750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508579#post1508579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't always work:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, you can embrace 50 more vamps a night, but would they fight and die for you? Do you think some would run and hide, or others, betray you so the Lupines may spare them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Dominate and Presence help, so does the blood bond. And vampire who needs somewhat hardened, loyal troops fast could make something of a sacrifice by embracing all of its Herd and Retainers, many of whom are possibly already bonded and familiar with the supernatural to a degree, for example.<br /> <br /> Ruthlessness is everything in Jyhad escalation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508579#post1508579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you're right about Lupines; it will take a long time to replenish their ranks, so, better set up an ambush rather than a siege and or get someone else to siege the city, like an Allied Bombing raid.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou more than anyone have to be very careful with how they spend or sacrifice their resources - that nine times out of ten also happen to be one's allies, closest friends and family, so every loss can hurt all that much on a personal level.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T09:07:31-07:00","id":1509042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1508723#post1508723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of the usual, normal, prepared, and experienced construction crews another approach could be decided upon. My idea is that it could be attempted that groups of mortal volunteers, maybe standard workers, or honest amateurs could be drafted or employed into various logistics, structures, and terrain related tasks, projects, and activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you can get a lot done with rank-and-file workers, the issue of scale and quality are what puts vampiric defenses in the realm of proper construction crews.<br /> <br /> When mortals build, at least here in America, the infrastructure is rated to last about 50 years and often barely makes it even half that. A vampire has no functional lifespan, so if you want the structure to last longer, then you need both better materials and techniques for building with them. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, we have to consider vampiric parameters when it comes to threats. A relatively thin concrete wall will stop a human, but it can't be assumed to stop a Potence 5/Strength 5 vampire who being somewhat cranky. That would require a double thickness concrete pour and lots of rebar reinforcement, and even then the vampire could possibly crack the wall enough to allow for a Discipline alternative form like mist, blood, or shadow to seep through.<br /> <br /> Going back to fortifying a business building, its not like there really is such a thing as an amateur elevator technician to modify the safety functions so you can remotely drop the elevator when invaders decide to skip the cardio of running up the stairs for 20+ floors. Though I could see an amateur being able to rig something like a halon fire extinguisher system on each elevator so you can choke out mortal attackers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T09:31:38-07:00","id":1509047,"title":"","content":"We are trying it now in our game with a rogue Ventrue Archon who is a great grand childe of Hardstadt the Younger who is targeting the Brujah leaders that are of Tyler's lineage and so far it's mostly cat &amp; mouse with my Brujah character keeping an eye on his mortal descendants welfare and doing his job as a bodyguard for the Baron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T04:20:01-07:00","id":1509163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509042#post1509042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While you can get a lot done with rank-and-file workers, the issue of scale and quality are what puts vampiric defenses in the realm of proper construction crews.<br /> <br /> When mortals build, at least here in America, the infrastructure is rated to last about 50 years and often barely makes it even half that. A vampire has no functional lifespan, so if you want the structure to last longer, then you need both better materials and techniques for building with them.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, we have to consider vampiric parameters when it comes to threats. A relatively thin concrete wall will stop a human, but it can't be assumed to stop a Potence 5/Strength 5 vampire who being somewhat cranky. That would require a double thickness concrete pour and lots of rebar reinforcement, and even then the vampire could possibly crack the wall enough to allow for a Discipline alternative form like mist, blood, or shadow to seep through.<br /> <br /> Going back to fortifying a business building, its not like there really is such a thing as an amateur elevator technician to modify the safety functions so you can remotely drop the elevator when invaders decide to skip the cardio of running up the stairs for 20+ floors. Though I could see an amateur being able to rig something like a halon fire extinguisher system on each elevator so you can choke out mortal attackers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the extinguisher's a safer choice in the long run, unless the vampire always uses the stairs (being undead, they have the stamina for it)<br /> <br /> Supernaturals can readily overcome a good lot of barriers with relative ease. Things that mortals wouldn't dare climb can be very easy for relatively low-level werewolves and vampires. But it's also important not to overcorrect. You and your retainers can be killed by your own traps or stuck in/outside your own haven. chokepoints you planned to utilize can very handily be used by your enemy. A rival can very handily off a paranoid vampire by modifying their security system, no questions would be asked, and the most elaborate pathway can be ignored by a frenzy. Ideally a vampire should be asking &quot;could this kill me instead?&quot; There's a lot that will kill or incapacitate a human but not a vampire, and it would be wise for vampires to tailor their traps for their stamina + fortitude levels. I'm fond of electricity and no-oxygen environments, silver BBs, climbs, and swims for emergencies, though really a good bit of open distance to confound obfuscate, nightingale floors and dominated guards are what most settle with. It's not good for a Ventrue's dignity to channel their inner Nosferatu, they might have guests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-21-2023, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:28:45-07:00","id":1509198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509163#post1509163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fond of electricity and no-oxygen environments, silver BBs, climbs, and swims for emergencies, though really a good bit of open distance to confound obfuscate, nightingale floors and dominated guards are what most settle with. It's not good for a Ventrue's dignity to channel their inner Nosferatu, they might have guests.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tricky thing is that it really depends on what you want the defensive work to accomplish. A series of vault doors and reinforced walls which would take heavy machinery and 8+ hours to bore through won't harm enemies, but it will take so long to get through that the sun will either go down or come up before they can get through it all.<br /> <br /> As for the Ventrue channeling their inner Nosferatu regarding security and guests, I feel that the Ventrue would have an ultra-secure haven, but then meet guests at a secondary location that is slightly less secure. The Ventrue are the archetypal vampires who own everything after all, why not have multiple buildings with each modified to your needs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:34:01-07:00","id":1509200,"title":"","content":"Or numerous safehouses that can be used in such situations or by paraniod elders who don't want to give rivals a predictable place to strike at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T23:55:27-07:00","id":1509260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509200#post1509200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or numerous safehouses that can be used in such situations or by paraniod elders who don't want to give rivals a predictable place to strike at.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my current game the Prince owns different almost identical Havens all around the city. He never plans which one he will use in advance, and only tells his driver in time to make it there comfortably enough at the end of the night. <br /> This came up during a story in which the Prince had been kidnapped from one of these havens during the day and how the kidnapper knew which one to attack was an important point in the investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:10:55-07:00","id":1509277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509260#post1509260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my current game the Prince owns different almost identical Havens all around the city. He never plans which one he will use in advance, and only tells his driver in time to make it there comfortably enough at the end of the night.<br /> This came up during a story in which the Prince had been kidnapped from one of these havens during the day and how the kidnapper knew which one to attack was an important point in the investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>GPS luggage tracker on the car?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:38:20-07:00","id":1509282,"title":"","content":"Switching havens all the time as a security measure is high foolishness. You're wasting resources, telegraphing all the backup plans you have, and setting yourself up for failure since you really just need to install one tripmine and the guy'll fall one day or another. You have one really well managed haven, and then you have secret emergency havens you fall back to. If you're well-to-do and don't have so many enemies there's nothing wrong with having a well run second or third haven for convenience or to display wealth but it's<i> not </i>a security benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:14:32-07:00","id":1509286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509282#post1509282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Switching havens all the time as a security measure is high foolishness. You're wasting resources, telegraphing all the backup plans you have, and setting yourself up for failure since you really just need to install one tripmine and the guy'll fall one day or another. You have one really well managed haven, and then you have secret emergency havens you fall back to. If you're well-to-do and don't have so many enemies there's nothing wrong with having a well run second or third haven for convenience or to display wealth but it's<i> not </i>a security benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond a certain level, Resources are endless, so wasting of resources is functionally a moot point.<br /> <br /> As for a trip mine, Vampires are unlikely to be killed by anti-personnel mines since they are designed to maim rather than kill mortals, so you would have to either use an anti-vehicle mine or rig an improvised incendiary trap, both of which have implementation issues.<br /> <br /> The anti-vehicle mine while directional requires the target be directly on top of it, which means unless you are in a rural area with dirt roads, someone will notice you jackhammering the vampire's driveway to install it, not to mention that unless you are controlling it by remote trigger, the mine isn't going to be discriminating in what triggers it. So, the mailman, the amazon driver, the ghoul who drives up to check on the property, or the mortal security service will all trigger it long before the vampire ever gets there. The scene in the first Godfather movie where the wife sets off the car bomb meant for Michael comes to mind.<br /> <br /> As for the incendiary trap, the tricky thing is hiding the incendiary materials from sight. You have to have enough material to create a fireball big enough to cover the distance from the hiding spot to the tripwire/trigger, most vampires will notice a 55-gallon drum of gasoline sitting on their front porch even if they can't see the tripwire. Sure, there are other materials that burn hotter and take up less space and thus could theoretically be hidden closer to the tripwire, but they are much harder to get ahold of and don't explode in huge plumes of fire like gasoline does. White Phosphorous for example burns very hot and will melt a vampire in short order, but it doesn't create a fireball, which means the delivery system needs a different set up than a tripwire. As with the anti-vehicle mine usage, this is likewise contingent on no one other than the vampire coming up to the house in question.<br /> <br /> On the subject of switching Havens, unless you are playing a character like a Nosferatu who lives outside of the public view, you technically should be changing Havens every 10 years or so to keep the masquerade intact since people will notice you are not aging. Unless you want to move out of the city, that means you have to maintain several potential havens to use in rotation, not returning to any given neighborhood for at least 20-40 years. That easily works out to three maybe four Havens just for time rotation, then a couple more that are hidden in case of emergencies, and then finally one or two in different cities in case things go to FUBAR levels of trouble. It is far simpler to buy all of these properties early on and switch between them, rather than trying to buy and sell them every decade.<br /> <br /> I know that turning VtM into a property management sim isn't what most people think of, but in truth, unless you are playing a wandering character like a Gangrel that just Earth Melds wherever there is open space, you kind of have to think in these terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:26:00-07:00","id":1509289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509277#post1509277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> GPS luggage tracker on the car?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would have worked but the culprit was an Elder using Spirit Magic and using a Wind elemental (quite prominent in Chicago)))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:26:49-07:00","id":1509290,"title":"","content":"I think you're overthinking the mine thing, it's just an example: you can do a whole bunch of things like fiddle with locks, change passwords, add more entrances, install cameras, mess with traps... that and it's not terribly hard to increase the yield of an explosive device or indeed use something properly incendiary like napalm, thermite or willy pete. Timed explosives are a good option too. <br /> <br /> resources might be virtually infinite but keeping secrets doesn't scale that well. The bigger and more complicated your operation, the more things can go wrong. Changing havens every night just creating a host of vulnerabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:32:49-07:00","id":1509292,"title":"","content":"I'd would go with a main haven myself, but I would make sure that I would have a couple of back up spots in case I pissed off a powerful elder or a crew of experienced hunters when the need arise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T19:35:36-07:00","id":1509340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509290#post1509290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're overthinking the mine thing, it's just an example: you can do a whole bunch of things like fiddle with locks, change passwords, add more entrances, install cameras, mess with traps... that and it's not terribly hard to increase the yield of an explosive device or indeed use something properly incendiary like napalm, thermite or willy pete. Timed explosives are a good option too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a case of overthinking, so much as practical understanding.<br /> <br /> Napalm is a jellied incendiary which doesn't really explode on its own, it is incredibly sticky and burns. It requires a proper dispersal device/secondary explosive to hit an area. Pouring burning napalm on a car won't do anything but ruin the paint and given enough time melt the plastic parts it is touching.<br /> <br /> Thermite much like napalm isn't a standalone explosive, its just an incendiary. It burns at high temperatures, but that heat is condensed into an area only about as big as the volume of the Thermite. So, if you have a sandwich bag full of thermite, if you set it off, it will only burn what it is sitting on top of and cause radiant heat damage within a couple of feet.<br /> <br /> In the case of both types of incendiary chemicals, the amount of damage is contingent on the volume of the material. Thus, a small ziplock bag of the stuff will burn out in a flash, with minimal damage to the surroundings, while a large canister of such material could burn for minutes on end. But once again the implementation of such a large canister makes creating the trap at the targets home base beyond impractical.<br /> <br /> As for timed explosives, once again the implementation of such an attack is impractical. First you have to know which location the vampire is going to ahead of time to set everything up, you have to know exactly when it is safe to set it up, you have to know the exact travel time and arrival time so you can trigger the timer and leave before the vampire shows up, and even with all of that, if you are off by as little as 30 seconds, the target will be out of position to be damaged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509290#post1509290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">resources might be virtually infinite but keeping secrets doesn't scale that well. The bigger and more complicated your operation, the more things can go wrong. Changing havens every night just creating a host of vulnerabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assumption is that the enemy has total knowledge of the entire system of havens. Using traps like this only work if the enemy doesn't know you are coming. If you poke around too much it tips them off, if you attempt to kill them and fail it tips them off. In both cases the target will then change their patterns and you are back to square one having no idea where they are or what they will do in response.<br /> <br /> I would also point out that historically, never spending too much time in any one location has proven to be effective against large agencies or militaries wanting to execute the individual in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T05:11:05-07:00","id":1509363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509198#post1509198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Ventrue channeling their inner Nosferatu regarding security and guests, I feel that the Ventrue would have an ultra-secure haven, but then meet guests at a secondary location that is slightly less secure. The Ventrue are the archetypal vampires who own everything after all, why not have multiple buildings with each modified to your needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it is clear this image and idea about Ventrue Vampires, that they have a definite tendency and inclination to exploiting and also using both influence as well reputation.<br /> They rely on these fields of interaction and methods in regard to multiple and varied activities.<br /> For example this tendency can be very distinct in regard to protection, street games, securing, military decisions and matters, espionage games, and expansion of wealth and resources.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T06:52:49-07:00","id":1509369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509198#post1509198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Ventrue channeling their inner Nosferatu regarding security and guests,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not totally out of the realm of possibility<br /> I mean, even the Ventrue Antediluvian took that route<br /> Well, at least by a nice forgotten lore-piece (Ventrue 1st ed CB: p 14-15 if anyone interested); back in the First City, Caine &quot;trusted&quot; the Ventrue Antediluvian enough to tell him about the Secret Masters...<br /> Even Caine feared them, and his warning made the Ventrue Antediluvian to turn his palace to a fortress in the First city and gather things like the head of Medusa, the claw of Fenris, and other powerfull relics of the age<br /> Not only that but the Ventrue believe that Caine himself has given Ventrue the imperative of <i>stopping </i>the Secret Masters, after he had witnessed the coming of great destruction for mankind from their hands. (The Ventrue Antediluvian was determined to free the Children of Seth from their subservience to these creatures....)\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T13:15:54-07:00","id":1509406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509340#post1509340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a case of overthinking, so much as practical understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Houses have been burnt down by cigarettes, are usually connected to gas pipes, and vampires are particularly vulnerable to sudden sun exposure. I'm sure we can play for hours trying to one-up eachother on why a particular mechanism or clever plan would or wouldn't work, but from my experience <i>things tend to work. </i> Maybe you can't always come up with some clever plan to kill them mid day, but it's a lot easier to destroy or compromise havens than it is to set them up. It's a lot easier to stage ambushes than it is to avoid them, especially if you're using a set number of routes. I'm sure if you've got plenty of resources to waste, elder disciplines, powerful and loyal subordinates, and an unreasonably meticulous plan, you might be able to create a multi-haven system safer than just one haven, but that's asking for the stars to align, really. For us non-methuselah, you're just asking for something to go wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your assumption is that the enemy has total knowledge of the entire system of havens. Using traps like this only work if the enemy doesn't know you are coming. If you poke around too much it tips them off, if you attempt to kill them and fail it tips them off. </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you know the enemy is coming and there isn't a god damn thing you can do about it. The enemy can also make feints or, if you're that kind of vampire, shit all over your prestige and dignity by trashing havens you can't properly protect. They'll have an easier time pillaging you; murdering your ghouls, stealing away your herd, abducting your prized retainer, hunting in your domain....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also point out that historically, never spending too much time in any one location has proven to be effective against large agencies or militaries wanting to execute the individual in question. </div> </div> </div>Indeed this is fantastic if you've got nothing to lose but your life, I think Malks and Nos can manage some decent holdings while doing this, but anyone else? Vampires are <i>dead bodies</i> during the day, their capabilities to move around are significantly weaker. Doing this kind of thing for most clans hurts their ability to accumulate resources and hold onto prestige and face which is significantly important in a society as cutthroat as the Camarilla, nevermind the Anarchs or Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-23-2023, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T09:40:03-07:00","id":1509485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509406#post1509406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Houses have been burnt down by cigarettes, are usually connected to gas pipes, and vampires are particularly vulnerable to sudden sun exposure. I'm sure we can play for hours trying to one-up eachother on why a particular mechanism or clever plan would or wouldn't work, but from my experience <i>things tend to work. </i> Maybe you can't always come up with some clever plan to kill them mid day, but it's a lot easier to destroy or compromise havens than it is to set them up. It's a lot easier to stage ambushes than it is to avoid them, especially if you're using a set number of routes. I'm sure if you've got plenty of resources to waste, elder disciplines, powerful and loyal subordinates, and an unreasonably meticulous plan, you might be able to create a multi-haven system safer than just one haven, but that's asking for the stars to align, really. For us non-methuselah, you're just asking for something to go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can houses be burnt down by cigarettes, sure, but at the same time how many vampires would set up their havens to be tinder boxes which go up in an inferno? What you are describing is very cinematic in nature, but sadly most movies create such situations just so they can have the flashy scene later on. Just having a house with tile floors, metal blinds on the windows, and a $100 exterior fire suppression sprinkler system makes most fire issues somewhat moot. <br /> <br /> It doesn't take that much money to own multiple pieces of property, back in the 90s it was still common to be able to get a house for less than $100,000 in California, if you were willing to purchase foreclosures and do a retrofit it was more like $60,000. Since we are talking about established vampires in this thread, they would have picked up the properties at an earlier time and for cheaper.<br /> <br /> I don't understand where you are getting this idea that owning multiple houses, which have been upgraded with a degree of security requires some sort of master plan. Once the purchase is complete and the upgrades are done, it just sits there until needed. At most you might have a ghoul do a daytime inspection every now and then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509406#post1509406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes you know the enemy is coming and there isn't a god damn thing you can do about it. The enemy can also make feints or, if you're that kind of vampire, shit all over your prestige and dignity by trashing havens you can't properly protect. They'll have an easier time pillaging you; murdering your ghouls, stealing away your herd, abducting your prized retainer, hunting in your domain....\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What you are describing is petty and useless. Prestige only matters to harpies as long as you survive and win. Havens can be repaired, sold off, or replaced as needed. Ghouls can be replaced, and your Herd cycles out as they age or die. As for them hunting in your Domain, that just means you have a home field advantage and know where they will be.<br /> <br /> Thinking like a functional vampire means you abandon thinking like a highschooler who is worried about not looking cool. Consider the Patrick Swayze movie Road House, in it he is a bouncer and he knows that he will piss people off. So rather than driving his nice car to work every night, he drives an old beater that he has no attachment to because he knows idiots will trash his car to get back at him. Sure he has to pay for repairs, but that is part of doing business. Property ownership can function the same way, you can own property that is specifically used and upgraded for idiot vampires to hurl themselves at, all the while your important stuff is safe.<br /> <br /> This isn't brain surgery or rocket science, it's basic business sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509406#post1509406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed this is fantastic if you've got nothing to lose but your life, I think Malks and Nos can manage some decent holdings while doing this, but anyone else? Vampires are <i>dead bodies</i> during the day, their capabilities to move around are significantly weaker. Doing this kind of thing for most clans hurts their ability to accumulate resources and hold onto prestige and face which is significantly important in a society as cutthroat as the Camarilla, nevermind the Anarchs or Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resource accumulation isn't a problem for Vampires, they have all of eternity to accumulate it. Where are you getting this head canon that it is difficult to accumulate wealth as a vampire? Yes you can start out as completely destitute, but between Blood Bonding, access to disciplines, and the fact you have eternity to lets things come to fruition, there is no real excuse to being a poor vampire other than lifestyle preference or mental limitation. Now if you want to play a character like that, more power to you, but don't confuse the potential way of building a character for the default when it puts you at a disadvantage for survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:32:28-07:00","id":1509491,"title":"","content":"...and then you sabotage the sprinkler system. <br /> <br /> Having a number of havens that people know about and which remain more lightly guarded is just a recipe for someone to come in and snoop in your home, maybe shuffle a few things around. Given the abilities of vampires, it's not hard to do things in ways you don't expect. Animalism, Dominate, Obfuscate, Necromancy, Thaumaturgy... Maybe a guard goes postal, or maybe the dogs don't bother the intruders tomorrow morning, or maybe there's a plethora of curses and wards waiting for you. It's much better to have one highly fortified haven which you rarely leave and which everything is intensely familiar to you than it is to have multiple you only kinda know . Keeping multiple havens in perfect condition is a waste of time, a waste of resources, and increases travel times. Remember you'll also want to have some modicum of control over the area around the haven as well as the haven itself. <br /> <br /> Having a bunch of emergency havens you hardly ever go to is a seperate thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T14:24:21-07:00","id":1509521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509491#post1509491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and then you sabotage the sprinkler system.<br /> <br /> Having a number of havens that people know about and which remain more lightly guarded is just a recipe for someone to come in and snoop in your home, maybe shuffle a few things around. Given the abilities of vampires, it's not hard to do things in ways you don't expect. Animalism, Dominate, Obfuscate, Necromancy, Thaumaturgy... Maybe a guard goes postal, or maybe the dogs don't bother the intruders tomorrow morning, or maybe there's a plethora of curses and wards waiting for you. It's much better to have one highly fortified haven which you rarely leave and which everything is intensely familiar to you than it is to have multiple you only kinda know . Keeping multiple havens in perfect condition is a waste of time, a waste of resources, and increases travel times. Remember you'll also want to have some modicum of control over the area around the haven as well as the haven itself.<br /> <br /> Having a bunch of emergency havens you hardly ever go to is a seperate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a sabotaged sprinkler system negate non-flammable building materials and fire prevention in decor choices? By stacking smart choices, the countering of any one thing doesn't lead to complete failure.<br /> <br /> Once again you are assuming every haven is public knowledge, which is erroneous as a starting point. Some havens can be large mansions, some can be small apartments, but others can simply be individual rooms that have been upgraded and hidden which are part of other businesses. A sub-basement area in a department store, a reinforced storage locker at a 24 hour storage facility, etc. Each of these add-on havens means that the business itself generates wealth, has its own security, and potentially gains you local influence depending on the business. Any attack to destroy your havens would very quickly be on a scale that would make the mortals believe a terror attack was happening, which in turn makes such an attack plan potentially be masquerade breaking.<br /> <br /> But for the sake of indulging your point of view, let's assume a singular bunker existence, rather than a randomized haven strategy. So every vampire lives in a decommissioned nuclear launch silo (initial purchase price is only about $350K) and it has been retrofitted to be anti-supernatural protected and allow for up to five years of underground existence without fresh supplies and a live in Herd.<br /> <br /> The only problem is that with such a vampiric society design, there is no such thing as Elysium, no such thing as Harpies, no functional prestige or reputation system. Basically all the stuff that is crowbarred into VtM to make plot hooks happen that you have been harping on about in previous posts no longer exist since every vampire is a self-contained unit and only interacts with other vampires via video call. Hunters can't track you because you never leave to feed or use the hunting grounds, rival factions don't really exist because every vampire becomes a shut in and it is way too dangerous to try to take territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T14:49:46-07:00","id":1509524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509491#post1509491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Keeping multiple havens in perfect condition is a waste of time, a waste of resources, and increases travel times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this idea ( or notion ) that it can be troublesome, problematic, or difficult to secure, upgrade, and improve multiple Havens or other locations that a Vampiress can use reliably for vital and important activities ( for example resting, planning, sleeping, and organizing entertainment ) . If a Vampiress is reliably good enough or simply perfect in regard to resolving and taking care of these issues and matters, then it can be done without unexpected risk and also with relatively low costs and payments.<br /> With clear intent and honest effort this can certainly be accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T20:33:49-07:00","id":1509682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509491#post1509491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and then you sabotage the sprinkler system.<br /> <br /> Having a number of havens that people know about and which remain more lightly guarded is just a recipe for someone to come in and snoop in your home, maybe shuffle a few things around. Given the abilities of vampires, it's not hard to do things in ways you don't expect. Animalism, Dominate, Obfuscate, Necromancy, Thaumaturgy... Maybe a guard goes postal, or maybe the dogs don't bother the intruders tomorrow morning, or maybe there's a plethora of curses and wards waiting for you. It's much better to have one highly fortified haven which you rarely leave and which everything is intensely familiar to you than it is to have multiple you only kinda know . Keeping multiple havens in perfect condition is a waste of time, a waste of resources, and increases travel times. Remember you'll also want to have some modicum of control over the area around the haven as well as the haven itself.<br /> <br /> Having a bunch of emergency havens you hardly ever go to is a seperate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you are the Prince of Chicago and the Sire of one of the richest vampires in North America, money is hardly a concern. <br /> <br /> If you only have one Haven you are more susceptible to being ambushed in your way there because there are fewer possible routes. Additionally, if you are followed in your way there, your potential attackers can craft a good assault plan in the certainty that you will be there every day. But if they lack that information, the whole planning becomes much more complicated. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T01:08:18-07:00","id":1509848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508459-have-you-defended-a-city?p=1509682#post1509682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you are the Prince of Chicago and the Sire of one of the richest vampires in North America, money is hardly a concern.<br /> <br /> If you only have one Haven you are more susceptible to being ambushed in your way there because there are fewer possible routes. Additionally, if you are followed in your way there, your potential attackers can craft a good assault plan in the certainty that you will be there every day. But if they lack that information, the whole planning becomes much more complicated.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If there is need for additional securing, ease of developing interests and projects, options in regard to research, and stability at a Haven of a Vampiress or a Vampire ( and also at the place or location in which the Home or Haven is placed ) , then it is good to remember and consider that status, fame, popularity, and reputation are clearly and definitely factors and qualities that contribute to peace, safety, stability, social interactions, and developing culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}